      "content": "okay, so the science part seems pretty settled then. but when you say the civil liberties side is about \"unwarranted government intrusion,\" doesn't that imply that their concerns might be unwarranted? like, if the scientific consensus is so strong and the goal is saving lives, isn't the \"burden of proof\" for the government naturally met, making the civil liberties arguments look more like they're just standing in the way of progress? i'm trying to figure out if the \"debate\" is actually between two valid viewpoints or if one side is just objectively right according to the evidence.",
